  "configuration_id": "config_028",
  "reason": "The dominant finding from the history is that switching the RNA encoder from scgpt to scvi_n200 (config_033: 0.706 acc) produced a ~16-point accuracy jump over the prior best (config_016: 0.542 acc), far exceeding any other single design change. However, we have only one data point with scvi_n200, and it is multimodal. The critical open question is whether the image modality (imagenet_vit_l, which alone scores only 0.227) is actually contributing to config_033's strong performance, or whether scvi_n200 RNA features alone are already sufficient. config_028 (rna_only, scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool) is a clean single-variable ablation of config_033—removing only the image branch while keeping the same RNA encoder and profile aggregation. If RNA-only performance is near 0.70, the image adds little and we can simplify; if it drops substantially, the multimodal fusion is genuinely valuable and we should next explore image encoder alternatives (e.g., resnet50 via config_027). Under a limited budget, resolving whether the image modality earns its complexity cost is the highest-information experiment before investing further in fusion or encoder variants."
}

